From 4c56f9cd3033e5f65ef9c61bc7b396d50bce23f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Kearney <303316+iconidentify@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:33:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rust: restore --no-layout-tests, make layout checks opt-in

Commit 97655bb70bc8 ("rust: check generated layouts and provide
corrected private bindgen") dropped the upstream --no-layout-tests flag
from cmd_bindgen. The generated bindings then carry bindgen's size,
alignment and offset assertions, and stock bindgen cannot build the
kernel any more: with the release configuration, `make prepare` fails
on the size of ns_common, pid_namespace, user_namespace and
cgroup_namespace with bindgen 0.73.2, and additionally task_struct,
zone and pglist_data with 0.73.1. Our release recipe builds with the
distribution's stock rust-bindgen, so the package build breaks.

These are size-only mismatches at the end of the types: every offset
and alignment assertion passes. The .19 release builds the same
mismatches, with the assertions not generated.

Pass --no-layout-tests again by default, as upstream does, so the
bindgen command line matches .19 again. Building with
`make BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1` drops the flag and keeps the assertions,
so the private generator in tools/aurora-bindgen can still be used to
check a configuration. Update the documentation and the recipe's hint
to describe that.

Verified with the release configuration (olddefconfig), ARCH=arm64
LLVM=1 W=1: `make prepare` and `make rust/` succeed with no warnings
using /usr/bin/bindgen 0.73.1 and using unpatched upstream bindgen
0.73.2. With BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1 both stop with E0080 size errors on
the types above; with the patched generator from tools/aurora-bindgen,
all 36943 assertions build. Switching the variable regenerates the
bindings.

Signed-off-by: Chris Kearney <303316+iconidentify@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst | 107 +++++++++++--------
 rust/Makefile                                |  15 ++-
 tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst              |  28 +++--
 tools/aurora-bindgen/build.py                |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst b/Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst
index 8ad8c24526b672..aaac5b24fb742e 100644
--- a/Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst
+++ b/Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst
@@ -3,47 +3,66 @@
 Checking generated binding layouts
 ==================================
 
-Kernel bindings retain bindgen's layout checks. With the configured Rust target,
-these are unconditional constant assertions, checked while the bindings crate
-is compiled. They compare Rust sizes, alignments and field offsets against the
-values obtained from Clang, without executing kernel code.
-
-Do not disable these checks to make an incompatible binding generator compile.
-A type can have the right size and still have incorrect member offsets. For
-example, an empty GNU C struct may have size zero and alignment 64; losing that
-alignment moves later fields in an enclosing struct without necessarily
-changing the enclosing size.
-
-Known generator requirements
-----------------------------
-
-Unmodified bindgen 0.73.2 loses explicit alignment on defined zero-sized C
-structs. It also omits the named anonymous record member accepted by Clang's
-``-fms-extensions`` in a declaration such as::
-
-    struct payload { unsigned long words[20]; };
-    union container {
-        struct payload;
-        unsigned long other;
-    };
-
-The generator used for this tree must preserve these layouts. Use a corrected
-bindgen build through the normal ``BINDGEN=/path/to/bindgen`` make variable.
-``tools/aurora-bindgen/`` contains pinned patches, a private build recipe and
-compile-only valid-input tests. It never installs a system-wide tool. The
-associated build provenance must retain the generator source revision,
-patches, binary digest, and valid-input C/Rust layout checks. A version string
-alone does not identify a locally corrected tool. Do not add dummy kernel
-storage, hardcode task offsets, or change scheduler configuration to conceal a
-binding generator error.
-
-After a binding layout correction, rebuild the kernel Image and all matching
-modules. The generated bindings are consumed by the Rust kernel crate and by
-multiple drivers; rebuilding just one module can leave incompatible layouts in
-the same kernel. Keep the old Image and its own modules together as a fallback.
-
-The minimum accepted bindgen version is 0.71.1. Its Rust 1.77 ``offset_of``
-feature enables unconditional const layout assertions; the configured Rust
-target 1.85 selects that path rather than ``#[test]``-only functions. The pinned
-0.73.2 tool has the same behavior. See the source links and explicit target
-accounting in ``tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst``.
+bindgen can emit compile-time assertions that compare the size, alignment and
+field offsets of every generated Rust type with the values Clang computes for
+the C type. As upstream, the kernel build passes ``--no-layout-tests`` to
+bindgen, so the generated bindings do not contain these assertions and any
+supported bindgen version can build the kernel.
+
+To check the layouts of a configuration, build with ``BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1``::
+
+    make LLVM=1 BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1 prepare
+
+The bindings are then generated with the assertions, which are checked while
+the ``bindings`` and ``uapi`` crates are compiled; nothing is executed. A
+mismatch stops the build with an ``E0080`` error naming the type and the
+property (``Size of``, ``Alignment of`` or ``Offset of``). Changing the
+variable regenerates the bindings. The check covers only the configuration
+being built.
+
+Known generator limitations
+---------------------------
+
+Unmodified bindgen 0.73 does not reproduce every C layout used by the kernel:
+
+* It omits a named anonymous record member, which Clang accepts with
+  ``-fms-extensions``, in a declaration such as::
+
+      struct payload { unsigned long words[20]; };
+      union container {
+          struct payload;
+          unsigned long other;
+      };
+
+* It can drop the explicit alignment of a defined zero-sized C struct, such
+  as ``struct empty {} __attribute__((aligned(64)));``.
+
+With the assertions enabled and stock bindgen 0.73.2, an arm64 Apple
+silicon configuration of this tree fails on the size of ``ns_common`` and of
+the namespace structures that embed it; bindgen 0.73.1 also fails on
+``task_struct``, ``zone`` and ``pglist_data``. In those builds every offset
+and alignment assertion passes: bindgen pads each field to the offset Clang
+reports, so only the end of the Rust type is short. Rust code that reaches
+such a type through a pointer and reads its fields gets the right data, but
+must not rely on ``size_of`` for it, copy it by value or index an array of
+it. The affected types depend on the bindgen version and the configuration,
+which is what the check is for.
+
+Corrected generator
+-------------------
+
+``tools/aurora-bindgen/`` contains pinned patches for bindgen 0.73.2 that
+repair both cases, a private build recipe and compile-only tests; see
+``tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst``. It installs nothing system-wide. To check
+the layouts with it::
+
+    make LLVM=1 BINDGEN=/path/to/bindgen BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1 ...
+
+The generated bindings are consumed by the Rust kernel crate and by several
+drivers. After changing the bindings generator, rebuild the kernel Image and
+all modules together.
+
+The assertions need bindgen 0.71.1 or later (the kernel minimum) together with
+the configured ``--rust-target 1.85``: that selects unconditional constant
+assertions rather than ``#[test]`` functions, so a build with
+``BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1`` checks them without a Rust test configuration.
diff --git a/rust/Makefile b/rust/Makefile
index 2fee22bdb0e146..915d3a6f9e0b25 100644
--- a/rust/Makefile
+++ b/rust/Makefile
@@ -443,14 +443,23 @@ endif
 # architecture instead of generating `usize`.
 bindgen_c_flags_final = $(bindgen_c_flags_lto) -fno-builtin -D__BINDGEN__
 
+# Layout assertions are off by default, as upstream: stock bindgen 0.73
+# computes a different total size for a few kernel types, so the bindings
+# would not build with it. `make BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1` keeps them, for
+# checking a bindings generator; see
+# Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst.
+ifeq ($(BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS),1)
+bindgen_layout_flags :=
+else
+bindgen_layout_flags := --no-layout-tests
+endif
+
 # `--rust-target` points to our minimum supported Rust version.
-# Keep bindgen layout assertions enabled: a lost alignment can change field
-# offsets without changing the containing type size. See Documentation/rust/
-# bindgen-layout-checks.rst for generator requirements.
 quiet_cmd_bindgen = BINDGEN $@
       cmd_bindgen = \
 	$(BINDGEN) $< $(bindgen_target_flags) --rust-target 1.85 \
 		--use-core --with-derive-default --ctypes-prefix ffi \
+		$(bindgen_layout_flags) \
 		--no-debug '.*' --enable-function-attribute-detection \
 		-o $@ -- $(bindgen_c_flags_final) -DMODULE \
 		$(bindgen_target_cflags) $(bindgen_target_extra)
diff --git a/tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst b/tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst
index 2c560aa13f96e4..75d4c3a2480e74 100644
--- a/tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst
+++ b/tools/aurora-bindgen/README.rst
@@ -25,7 +25,10 @@ locked dependency graph is used, with at most two build jobs. ``--archive`` can
 supply an already downloaded source archive; its digest is still checked. The
 script builds and runs compile-only valid-input checks, then prints the exact
 ``BINDGEN=/absolute/path/to/bindgen`` make argument. It installs nothing globally.
-Use that argument for the complete kernel Image and matching modules build.
+The kernel build passes ``--no-layout-tests`` to bindgen unless
+``BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1`` is given, so add that variable to check layouts
+with the private tool, and build the complete kernel Image and matching
+modules with the same tool.
 Both scripts reject optimized Python (``-O``, ``-OO`` or ``PYTHONOPTIMIZE``)
 before creating output, since their validation assertions must remain enabled.
 
@@ -67,14 +70,16 @@ generator, and its changes and both tool digests belong in the build record.
 Repository guard and supported tool versions
 --------------------------------------------
 
-The kernel keeps bindgen layout checks enabled. Its minimum bindgen is 0.71.1,
-and its fixed ``--rust-target 1.85`` enables the ``offset_of`` feature (available
-from Rust 1.77). In both official 0.71.1 and the pinned 0.73.2 generator, that
-feature selects unconditional const size/alignment/offset assertions rather
-than ``#[test]`` functions. A normal bindings crate compile therefore checks
-layouts without requiring a Rust unit-test configuration. This is source-backed
-for the accepted minimum and pinned tool; future generator changes must retain
-that capability. Never remove the assertions to accept an incompatible tool.
+By default the kernel passes ``--no-layout-tests``, as upstream, so stock
+bindgen builds it; ``make BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1`` keeps the layout checks
+(see ``Documentation/rust/bindgen-layout-checks.rst``). Its minimum bindgen is
+0.71.1, and its fixed ``--rust-target 1.85`` enables the ``offset_of`` feature
+(available from Rust 1.77). In both official 0.71.1 and the pinned 0.73.2
+generator, that feature selects unconditional const size/alignment/offset
+assertions rather than ``#[test]`` functions. A bindings crate compile with
+``BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1`` therefore checks layouts without requiring a Rust
+unit-test configuration. This is source-backed for the accepted minimum and
+pinned tool; future generator changes must retain that capability.
 
 Primary sources:
 
@@ -82,5 +87,6 @@ Primary sources:
 * https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-bindgen/blob/v0.71.1/bindgen/codegen/mod.rs
 * https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-bindgen/tree/v0.73.2
 
-The complete kernel build remains the configuration-specific layout gate; these
-small generator fixtures do not replace it or establish runtime GPU stability.
+A complete kernel build with ``BINDGEN_LAYOUT_TESTS=1`` remains the
+configuration-specific layout check; these small generator fixtures do not
+replace it or establish runtime GPU stability.
